Draw one horizontal bar per target from \code{targets::tar_meta()}, with bar
length mapped to the target runtime (\code{seconds}) and fill mapped to the output
size (\code{Gb}). Because \code{tar_meta()} only stores the metadata of the
\strong{latest} build of each target, this figure summarizes the resource impact
of the \emph{last} pipeline run. Targets that emitted a warning during that run are
flagged with a red star.

This is the metadata-based companion of \code{\link{ga_autometric_lastrun}()}
(which reconstructs the same "last run" picture from an \code{autometric}
log) and of \code{\link{ga_targets_network}()} (which shows the dependency
structure).
